From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 07:04:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin: tidy the rear camera
 nodes

Follow-up to the rear S5KJN1 bring-up; no change to the tested capture
path.

 - pm8350c_l1 was inserted between the panel iovdd comment and the
   pm8350c_l2 node it documents.  Move that comment back above l2 and
   give l1 its own note as the S5KJN1 vddio rail.

 - Nothing sits behind CCI1 (the front camera is not part of this
   bring-up), so drop its enablement and assigned clocks.

 - The s5kjn1 driver never selects a pinctrl "sleep" state, so the
   pinctrl-1 entry and the two suspend states only it referenced were
   dead.  Keep the "default" state the pinctrl core applies at probe.

 - The CAMSS node has no reg-bearing children (only "ports"), so its
   #address-cells/#size-cells trip dtc's W=1 avoid_unnecessary_addr_size
   check.  Drop them here and from the binding and its example.

The vendor abl-final-fdt.dts was not available while preparing this
change, so whether PM8350C L1 has consumers besides the camera could not
be checked against it.  Describing L1 lets the regulator core switch it
off when the camera is idle, so any other L1 user would need to be
listed here as a consumer.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0119npaRT3BS6ioVvnE1XeMT
Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

